-- WAY W3 (not chosen): the reader's knowledge is applied OUTSIDE the version, by moving the date at which
-- the text is read.
--
-- The version rule reads `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` only, with no TODAY.  A selector decides which date to pin,
-- from the conduct day and the reading day: a reader before 31 October 2012 reads 2011 conduct "as at
-- 31 December 2010", the last day before the Notification's deemed commencement.
--
-- For ONE day it gives the same answers as the chosen way (the generated block).
-- Over a PERIOD it is wrong: ALWAYS BETWEEN and its siblings re-stamp the rule-effective axis to each stepped day
-- themselves, which overwrites the selector's clamp (the two directives under "Over a period").
-- And a caller that reaches the version rule directly, under a plain pin, bypasses the selector (the last one).
-- Printed output is in alt-w3-selector.out; walkthrough step 7.
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

DECLARE `Version of the First Schedule` IS ONE OF
    `the First Schedule of three items`
    `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`

`the text, read at the rule-effective date` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` BELOW (Date 31 7 2003)
           THEN REFUSE "not covered: the conduct day is before the first deposited edition (31 July 2003)"
           IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011)
           THEN `the First Schedule of the TVRO system only`
           OTHERWISE `the First Schedule of three items`

-- The selector: before 31 October 2012 the Notification is not yet visible, so read the text as at 31 December 2010.
GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the text is read at` MEANS
    IF reading BELOW (Date 31 10 2012) AND conduct AT LEAST (Date 1 1 2011) THEN Date 31 12 2010 ELSE conduct

GIVEN conduct IS A DATE
      reading IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of the First Schedule`
`the text under this way` MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (`the date the text is read at` conduct reading) `the text, read at the rule-effective date`

-- Over a period.  A reader of 1 August 2012 should find the 2011 days all under the three-item text.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the three-item text governs that day` MEANS
    `the text, read at the rule-effective date` EQUALS `the First Schedule of three items`

-- Over a period, 1 Jan 2011 to 31 Jan 2011, read on 1 August 2012, through the selector's pin: ALWAYS should be TRUE.
#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (`the date the text is read at` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 1 8 2012)) (`ALWAYS BETWEEN` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 31 1 2011) `the three-item text governs that day`)
-- Bypass: the version rule under a plain pin, for a reader of 1 August 2012 and conduct on 1 June 2011.
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 8 2012) (`EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2011) `the text, read at the rule-effective date`)

-- BEGIN GENERATED PAIRS (build-walkthrough.py: the same conduct-day and reading-day pairs in every file)
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 8 2012)   -- P01
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 31 10 2012)   -- P02
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 11 2012)   -- P03
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 1 1 2020)   -- P04
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 31 12 2010) (Date 1 8 2012)   -- P05
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 31 12 2010) (Date 1 11 2012)   -- P06
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 6 2011) (Date 30 10 2012)   -- P07
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 30 10 2012) (Date 1 11 2012)   -- P08
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 31 10 2012) (Date 1 11 2012)   -- P09
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 11 2012) (Date 1 11 2012)   -- P10
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 31 10 2012) (Date 30 10 2012)   -- P11
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 1 1 2011) (Date 1 11 2012)   -- P12
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 4 11 2026) (Date 4 11 2026)   -- P13
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 30 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026)   -- P14
#EVAL `the text under this way` (Date 31 7 2003) (Date 4 11 2026)   -- P15
-- END GENERATED PAIRS
